  {
   "d": "2022-10-04",
   "doc": "YE-TU",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -3,
   "q": "As a result, whilst H2-2022 performance was materially stronger than H1-2022, the Board now expects FY-2022 underlying operating profit to be c.10% below current market expectations.",
   "file": "20221004_WJG_FY-2022-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-01-25",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "However, we also believe it is prudent to assume that higher borrowing costs for our institutional clients will result in margin pressure continuing into FY23, and that new forward sales will be weighted to the second half of FY23.",
   "file": "20230125_WJG_Full-Year-Results-2022.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-04-13",
   "doc": "H1 TU",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "As previously flagged, performance will be materially H2 weighted.",
   "file": "20230413_WJG_H1-2023-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-05-23",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "Currently targeting up to five further forward sales in FY23, with full year earnings performance dependent on concluding these transactions in what remains a volatile environment, as well as finally agreed pricing and phasing terms",
   "file": "20230523_WJG_Half-Year-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-07-19",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -3,
   "q": "Our current expectation is that these challenging market conditions will persist into FY24, and against this more cautious backdrop, our FY24 PBIT is likely to be in the range of £15m to £20m.",
   "file": "20230719_WJG_Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-10-11",
   "doc": "YE-TU",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
